Mushin for AmigaOS 3.x / m68k
============================

Mushin is a MUI-compatible user interface library based on AROS Zune.
This package contains the core libraries and the opentest application.
It does not include the preferences editor, extra MCCs, or an SDK.

Requirements
------------
AmigaOS 3.1 or newer, a 68000 or better, and Amiga Installer 43 or newer.
The system IEEE double math libraries must be available; no FPU is needed.
Installer itself is not included. The Install icon uses
SYS:System/Installer, the location supplied with AmigaOS 3.2.3. If your
Installer is elsewhere, change the icon's Default Tool to its path.

Installation
------------
Extract the archive and double-click Install inside the Mushin drawer.
Alternatively, change to that drawer in a Shell and run:

  SYS:System/Installer Install MINUSER AVERAGE

Each library has its own Install/Skip question. Existing and bundled
versions are shown before anything is replaced. Versions come from the
actual files, not from the archive filename. Unknown versions are shown
as unknown. Equal-version replacements and downgrades require the same
explicit choice as upgrades. The default is Skip.

  zunemaster.library  -> LIBS:zunemaster.library
    Installs alongside MUI. opentest uses this name by default.

  muimaster.library   -> LIBS:muimaster.library
    Replaces MUI for applications using the standard library name.
    Installing this is optional; it can affect other MUI applications.

Before replacing a file, the installer saves the original beside it as
<library-name>.mushin-old. An existing backup is preserved. Copy or
rename that backup back to the original name to restore it. A newer
resident library can remain active until reboot; the installer reports
the resident version separately and does not expunge libraries in use.

The installer copies only libraries. Tests/opentest remains in the
extracted package. Nothing changes in S:Startup-Sequence or S:User-Startup.
Pretend mode displays the choices without copying files.

After installation, close applications and reboot before trying Mushin.
Run Tests/opentest from the extracted drawer. To exercise the replacement
name explicitly, run Tests/opentest muimaster.library.

The GNU-built opentest automatically requests at least 65536 bytes of
stack and frees any replacement stack on exit. For older or SAS/C-built
test programs, run Stack 65536 in the same Shell first.

Normal builds omit Zune drawing/input traces. The test still prints its
own progress and results. Source builds can enable tracing with TRACE=1;
that output is deliberately excluded from performance measurements.

Status and source
-----------------
This is a development build. Compiler and binary-interface checks do not
establish application compatibility or performance on real hardware.

Source: https://github.com/amigazen/mushin/
